Razavi-Bench Repository License Terms

Copyright (c) 2026 Zhang Tuoken.

This repository contains software code, benchmark materials, and third-party
source materials with different permission boundaries. The terms below apply
unless a separate written agreement says otherwise.

1. Scope

"Software code" means scripts, tooling, workflow files, and original website
implementation code whose primary purpose is to run, analyze, or display the
benchmark.

"Benchmark materials" means tasks, prompts, questions, figures, source PDFs,
golden solutions, evaluation rubrics, judge prompts, model outputs, score
tables, metadata, derived datasets, dashboard-embedded benchmark data,
documentation describing the benchmark, and any content adapted from Behzad
Razavi's articles.

Some files, such as dashboard HTML pages, contain both software/UI code and
embedded benchmark materials. The software/UI portions are covered by the
software license below; the embedded benchmark materials are covered by the
benchmark-materials terms below.

2. Source Material and Third-Party Rights

Razavi-Bench includes or adapts source questions and figures from Behzad
Razavi's "Analog Design Experiments With AI--Part 1 [The Analog Mind]" and
"Analog Design Experiments With AI--Part 2 [The Analog Mind]", published in
IEEE Solid-State Circuits Magazine.

Those source materials are included or adapted in this repository with
permission from Behzad Razavi. That permission does not grant third parties any
right to redistribute, sublicense, republish, rehost, mirror, sell, or repackage
the source materials or adapted benchmark materials. Original article,
question, and figure copyrights remain with their respective rights holders,
including Behzad Razavi and/or IEEE, as applicable.

3. Benchmark Materials

The benchmark materials are made available for public viewing, citation,
non-commercial research reference, and local evaluation from this repository.
You may publish aggregate evaluation results produced using Razavi-Bench,
provided that you cite this repository and do not redistribute the benchmark
materials themselves.

You may not, without prior written permission from the project maintainers and
any applicable rights holders:

- copy, redistribute, sublicense, rehost, mirror, republish, sell, or otherwise
  distribute the benchmark materials;
- incorporate the benchmark materials into a third-party benchmark, dataset,
  leaderboard, training set, fine-tuning set, evaluation suite, or packaged
  data release;
- use the benchmark materials to train or fine-tune models;
- remove or obscure attribution, source, copyright, or permission notices.

For permission requests, open an issue or contact the project maintainers.

4. Software Code

Software code in this repository is licensed under the Apache License, Version
